# Build-context hygiene (E11 FR-1, design D2). This file is a DENYLIST of
# patterns anchored at the context root. The three build stages COPY exactly
# web/, engine/, migrations/, src/, data/, and the Cargo + npm manifests;
# the patterns below keep VCS history, build outputs, and repo-only
# docs/specs/tooling out of what `docker build` uploads. A root path not
# named here DOES enter the context — it is simply never COPYed, so it
# never reaches a layer.

# VCS — the image builds from a git checkout; git history never enters it.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Build outputs and dependency trees — rebuilt inside the stages, never
# shipped in from the host (a host target/ or node_modules would also be
# the wrong architecture half the time).
target/
**/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Repo-only artifacts: documents, specs, integration tests, operator and CI
# tooling. None of it is COPYed by the Dockerfile.
docs/
specs/
tests/
scripts/
licenses/
.github/
.specify/
